  "steps": [
    "<strong>Roast the Sweet Potatoes:</strong> Heat oven to 220°C / 425°F. Toss sweet potatoes with olive oil, cayenne (if using), and salt. Spread on a lined tray and roast 30–40 minutes, turning halfway, until tender and caramelised.",
    "<strong>Cook the Beans:</strong> Heat olive oil in a saucepan over medium heat. Add onion with a pinch of salt and cook 5–8 minutes until soft.",
    "Add cumin and chilli powder; cook 30 seconds. Add beans and water, cover, and simmer 5 minutes.",
    "Uncover and mash roughly half the beans for a creamy, cohesive texture. Remove from heat, stir in vinegar or lime juice, and season well.",
    "<strong>Make the Sauce:</strong> Toast pepitas in a dry pan until fragrant and lightly popping. Cool slightly.",
    "Blend avocados, coriander, jalapeño, garlic, lime juice, water, salt, and pepper until smooth. Pulse in most of the pepitas, leaving some texture. Adjust seasoning.",
    "<strong>Warm Tortillas:</strong> Warm tortillas in a dry pan or directly over a low flame until pliable.",
    "<strong>Assemble:</strong> Spoon beans onto tortillas, top with roasted sweet potatoes, and finish with avocado-pepita sauce. Add feta (if using) and any optional toppings."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Mashing beans slightly is key — it stops tacos from feeling dry.",
    "The pepita sauce should be spoonable, not pourable.",
    "Pickled elements aren’t optional in spirit — they balance the richness."
  ]
